x86_64-linux  every special member here is written inside its class and is inline by nature, so clang emits one comdat copy and no C1/D1 at all where cxx1 emits both of Itanium's forms - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol". The same rule covers V::f and the two vtables: clang folds a vtable into the unit that defines the class's key function, cxx1 emits it wherever it sees the class. Nothing here is about layout, which is what the case checks and what its static_asserts pin on all three targets
arm64-darwin  same, and it is the same seven names: NP's implicit constructor and destructor in both of Itanium's forms, V::f, and the vtables of V and VD
x86_64-windows  same in kind, in Microsoft's spelling: ??0NP@@QEAA@XZ and ??1NP@@QEAA@XZ for the implicit special members, ?f@V@@UEAAXXZ for the inline virtual, and the two vftables ??_7V@@6B@ and ??_7VD@@6B@ - all of which cl and clang fold or omit and cxx1 emits, none of which is what this case measures
